  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/vieja-breidohri-2/",
      "html": "<p>Hans-Günther Breidohr (1938-2017) was one of the traveling aquarists who explored Central American cichlids in the 1980s and 1990s. In his honor Uwe Werner and Rainer Stawikowski named a cichlid Paratheraps breidohri, which was discovered on such trips and recognized as a new species due to the subsequent aquarium care. Today it is placed in the genus Vieja, so it is called Vieja breidohri.</p><p>Vieja breidohri grows 25-30 cm long, so it belongs to the large cichlids. Juveniles are still somewhat inconspicuous in color.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/vieja-breidohri-2/",
      "html": "<p>This cichlid is apparently very rarely found in the wild. It is only known from a reservoir in Chiapas, Mexico.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/vieja-breidohri-2/",
      "html": "<p>You only need to offer them enough space, then you can enjoy these character fish for many years.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/vieja-breidohri-2/",
      "html": "<p>It is strongly discouraged to combine different Vieja species with each other, as they can hybridize.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/vieja-breidohri-2/",
      "html": "<p>As usual in the Cichlasoma relatives, they are open breeders with parent family.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/vieja-breidohri-2/",
      "html": "<p>Existing strains need to be kept pure in conservation breeding.</p>"
    }
  ],
